1
00:00:00,490 --> 00:00:04,503
This might be the most dangerous
cell in this man's entire body.

2
00:00:04,543 --> 00:00:08,130
And the terrifying part is that
it used to be completely normal.

3
00:00:08,170 --> 00:00:12,690
Deep inside its nucleus, tiny mistakes
have been building up in its DNA.

4
00:00:12,730 --> 00:00:14,903
The instructions
controlling when it grows,

5
00:00:14,943 --> 00:00:18,117
when it stops, and when it
dies are starting to fail.

6
00:00:18,157 --> 00:00:21,250
And eventually, something
goes horribly wrong.

7
00:00:21,290 --> 00:00:23,143
The cell divides when it shouldn't.

8
00:00:23,183 --> 00:00:25,517
It ignores signals telling it to stop.

9
00:00:25,557 --> 00:00:27,570
And when the body tries to destroy it...

10
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:29,010
it survives.

11
00:00:29,050 --> 00:00:30,690
One cell becomes two.

12
00:00:30,730 --> 00:00:32,130
Two become four.

13
00:00:32,170 --> 00:00:36,100
Four become thousands and
this is how cancer begins.

14
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:37,730
But it gets worse.

15
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:42,360
The growing tumor steals nutrients,
recruits blood vessels to feed itself,

16
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:45,370
and even finds ways to hide
from the immune system.

17
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:47,880
Then some cancer cells break free.

18
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:50,320
They enter the bloodstream,
travel through the body,

19
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:53,600
and can create new tumors in
completely different organs.

20
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:55,650
And that's the real nightmare.

21
00:00:55,744 --> 00:00:57,360
Cancer isn't one enemy.

22
00:00:57,400 --> 00:01:00,640
It's millions of your own
cells, constantly changing,

23
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:03,610
evolving, and finding new ways to survive.

24
00:01:03,930 --> 00:01:07,500
But what if we could predict exactly
what those cells will do next?

25
00:01:07,570 --> 00:01:10,820
This is where artificial
intelligence changes the game.

26
00:01:11,170 --> 00:01:13,010
Imagine taking a patient's medical scans,

27
00:01:13,050 --> 00:01:16,210
tumor samples, and genetic
information, and using AI

28
00:01:16,250 --> 00:01:18,490
to construct a detailed
digital copy of their

29
00:01:18,530 --> 00:01:21,770
cancer which would create
a virtual battlefield.

30
00:01:21,810 --> 00:01:26,010
Inside that simulation, researchers could
test treatment strategies, predict how the

31
00:01:26,050 --> 00:01:30,650
tumor might respond, and search for its weaknesses before choosing how to attack it.

32
00:01:30,690 --> 00:01:33,810
Instead of treating every cancer
the same way, the treatment could

33
00:01:33,850 --> 00:01:37,620
be designed around the exact
tumor growing inside that person.

34
00:01:37,730 --> 00:01:40,860
But identifying the weakness
is only the beginning.

35
00:01:41,147 --> 00:01:43,930
AI can help scientists
design molecules that target

36
00:01:43,970 --> 00:01:47,180
the proteins cancer cells
depend on to survive.

37
00:01:47,397 --> 00:01:50,810
Imagine microscopic drug carriers
traveling through the bloodstream,

38
00:01:50,850 --> 00:01:52,837
recognizing markers on cancer cells,

39
00:01:52,877 --> 00:01:56,050
and delivering their deadly
payload directly to the tumor.

40
00:01:56,090 --> 00:02:00,627
Like guided missiles, operating at a
scale smaller than anything you can see.

41
00:02:00,667 --> 00:02:01,570
The goal?

42
00:02:01,610 --> 00:02:05,263
Destroy the cancer while sparing
as much healthy tissue as possible.

43
00:02:05,303 --> 00:02:06,730
But there's still a problem.

44
00:02:06,770 --> 00:02:10,570
Some cancer cells can survive,
mutate, and become resistant.

45
00:02:10,610 --> 00:02:12,860
So AI needs another weapon.

46
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:16,713
Your body already has an army
capable of killing cancer.

47
00:02:16,753 --> 00:02:18,500
It's called your immune system.

48
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:22,740
The problem is that cancer can disguise
itself, suppress immune defenses,

49
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:25,513
or become difficult for
those cells to recognize.

50
00:02:25,553 --> 00:02:28,580
But tumors can carry unique
molecular fingerprints.

51
00:02:28,620 --> 00:02:31,740
AI can help identify those
fingerprints and guide personalized

52
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:35,270
cancer vaccines or specialized
immune-cell treatments.

53
00:02:35,420 --> 00:02:38,580
Imagine your own T cells
learning exactly what to hunt.

54
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:40,460
They recognize a cancer cell.

55
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:41,433
Lock onto it.

56
00:02:41,473 --> 00:02:42,660
And destroy it.

57
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:44,420
Then they move to the next.

58
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:45,620
And the next.

59
00:02:45,660 --> 00:02:48,340
Suddenly, the tumor isn't
just fighting a drug,

60
00:02:48,380 --> 00:02:50,870
It's fighting the body's own defenses.

61
00:02:51,090 --> 00:02:54,570
But destroying the visible
tumor is only half the battle.

62
00:02:54,610 --> 00:02:57,210
Because even a tiny
population of surviving cancer

63
00:02:57,250 --> 00:02:59,770
cells can eventually
bring the disease back.

64
00:02:59,810 --> 00:03:02,410
And this is where things
get really interesting.

65
00:03:02,450 --> 00:03:06,456
Cancer can leave microscopic traces
of its DNA in the bloodstream.

66
00:03:06,496 --> 00:03:10,930
By analyzing these signals, AI could
help detect signs of a returning tumor,

67
00:03:10,970 --> 00:03:13,090
identify how it's
changing, and guide a new

68
00:03:13,130 --> 00:03:15,439
treatment before it grows out of control.

69
00:03:15,479 --> 00:03:18,860
An evolving enemy, met
by an evolving defense.

70
00:03:19,276 --> 00:03:22,190
And that's the breakthrough
behind this entire idea.

71
00:03:22,230 --> 00:03:25,030
Cancer isn't one disease
with one weakness.

72
00:03:25,070 --> 00:03:26,870
Every tumor can be different.

73
00:03:26,910 --> 00:03:30,630
So imagine a system that
doesn't need one universal drug.

74
00:03:30,670 --> 00:03:35,030
It studies each cancer, predicts its
behavior, designs a targeted attack,

75
00:03:35,070 --> 00:03:39,110
activates the immune system, and
watches for anything that survives.

76
00:03:39,150 --> 00:03:41,510
A different answer for every cancer.

77
00:03:41,550 --> 00:03:44,200
And remember that single
cell we started with?

78
00:03:44,361 --> 00:03:45,483
Imagine finding it...

79
00:03:45,523 --> 00:03:48,120
before it ever has the
chance to become a tumor.
